---
// COPY.md §2. Each card carries a small UI fragment built in HTML, not an image.
---

<section class="section problem" id="problem">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow problem-mark"><span>The problem</span></p>
      <h2>Your systems disagree with each other.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Every tool is good at its job. The trouble is everything in between.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card" data-reveal>
        <h3>Stock is wrong somewhere.</h3>
        <p>
          Your inventory system says 12. Your storefront says 9. The warehouse says 7. Someone
          reconciles it by hand every week, and you still oversell.
        </p>
        <div class="fragment" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="counts">
            <span><i>Cin7</i><b>12</b></span>
            <span><i>WooCommerce</i><b>9</b></span>
            <span class="is-off"><i>Warehouse</i><b>7</b></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card" data-reveal>
        <h3>Sales can't see orders.</h3>
        <p>
          Your CRM knows the deal closed but not that the order is stuck in production. Your reps
          find out when the customer calls.
        </p>
        <div class="fragment" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="deal">
            <span class="deal-name">Harbor Hotel Group</span>
            <span class="chip is-ok">Closed won</span>
          </div>
          <div class="deal deal-order">
            <span class="deal-name">Order #3039</span>
            <span class="chip is-warn">Stuck in production</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card" data-reveal>
        <h3>Every sync is something that breaks.</h3>
        <p>
          Connectors, Zaps and CSV exports hold it all together until an update breaks one and nobody
          notices for a week.
        </p>
        <div class="fragment" aria-hidden="true">
          <pre class="log"><span>02:14  sync woocommerce → cin7   ok</span>
<span>03:14  sync woocommerce → cin7   ok</span>
<span class="is-bad">04:14  sync woocommerce → cin7   failed</span>
<span class="is-bad">       auth token expired, 0 retries</span></pre>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="closing" data-reveal>
      You're paying for three subscriptions, the connectors between them, and the hours your team
      spends fixing what falls through.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem { --problem-red: #dc2626; background: var(--bg-subtle); }

  /* The label strikes through in red as the section arrives: the rule wipes left to right, keyed
     off the reveal class the section head already gets, so it fires in step with the fade. */
  .problem-mark { position: relative; display: inline-block; color: var(--problem-red); }
  .problem-mark span { position: relative; }
  .problem-mark::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0.12em;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--problem-red);
    transform: scaleX(0);
    transform-origin: left center;
    transition: transform 0.65s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) 0.25s;
  }
  .section-head.is-visible .problem-mark::after { transform: scaleX(1); }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .problem-mark::after { transition: none; transform: scaleX(1); }
  }

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 28px;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    transition: border-color 0.18s var(--ease);
  }
  .card:hover { border-color: var(--border-strong); }
  .card h3 { max-width: 22ch; }
  .card p { font-size: 0.9375rem; }

  .fragment {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 18px;
  }

  /* fragment 1: three sources, three numbers */
  .counts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 8px; }
  .counts span {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }
  .counts i {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .counts b {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .counts .is-off b { color: var(--danger); }
  .counts .is-off { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 35%, var(--border)); }

  /* fragment 2: a deal and its order, disagreeing */
  .deal {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .deal + .deal { margin-top: 6px; }
  .deal-name { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  .deal-order .deal-name { color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }
  .chip {
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 0;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .chip.is-ok { background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent-strong); }
  .chip.is-warn {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 14%, transparent);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 78%, var(--text));
  }

  /* fragment 3: the sync log that nobody reads */
  .log {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .log span { display: block; white-space: pre; }
  .log .is-bad { color: var(--danger); }

  .closing {
    margin: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px) auto 0;
    max-width: 60ch;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.56;
    color: var(--text-body);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .fragment { margin-top: 4px; }
  }
</style>
